<SiteLayout title="Questions — Dawnlight Labs" path="/faq" description="Answers about Dawnlight Labs, project availability, the website illustrations and getting in touch.">
<article class="shell legal-page"><header class="page-opening"><p class="context">Questions</p><h1>A little more<br/>about Dawnlight.</h1></header><div class="legal-copy">
  <section class="legal-section"><h2>What is Dawnlight Labs?</h2><p>An independent research laboratory in India exploring intelligence, computing and emerging hardware. Read <a href="/about">about the laboratory and its founders</a> or explore our <a href="/research">research interests</a>.</p></section>
  <section class="legal-section"><h2>Can I use the projects today?</h2><p>Each <a href="/projects">project page</a> describes its current status. OSCAR and KineTable are in development. Takokit and AiSH are active projects. These pages introduce the work; they do not provide a hosted product or imply that a public download is available.</p></section>
  <section class="legal-section"><h2>Are the interactive examples live products?</h2><p>They are illustrations designed to explain each project. Takokit does not record your voice, AiSH does not execute commands, OSCAR does not start Workers and KineTable does not simulate electrical behaviour. You can explore the examples without supplying personal data.</p></section>
  <section class="legal-section"><h2>How can I discuss a project or collaboration?</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:contact@dawnlightlabs.com">contact@dawnlightlabs.com</a>. Tell us what you are working on and which project or question interests you. Our <a href="/contact">contact page</a> also lets you copy the address.</p></section>
  <section class="legal-section"><h2>What information does this website collect?</h2><p>There are no accounts, payments or message forms. Production visitor statistics use Vercel Web Analytics. Details about hosting, analytics and email enquiries are in our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p></section>
</div></article>
</SiteLayout>
